{{!-- Turning the wheel — one control, quiet until the table is ready to use it.

      This was the tab's largest element: a four-step panel, always open, at the top. But turning the
      season happens ONCE per season and everything else on this tab is used THROUGHOUT one, so the
      loudest thing on the page was the thing you need least often, and what the table actually works
      with sat below it. It is a disclosure now, and what it holds is only what is done AT the turn.

      What it does NOT hold: the season's own results and its moments. Those are owed by the season
      the steading is IN — autumn's harvest was owed when autumn began — while this control is about
      LEAVING it. Both used to sit in one panel, which is why it could be headed "Winter" while the
      line under it said "Autumn, year 3". The control names the ACT now, and everything about the
      season you are in is in "During autumn", where it belongs.

      Only the INCOMING season's move is here, and rolling it is what turns the wheel — there is no
      separate "advance", because advancing and rolling are one act.

      Params: seasons (SeasonsSnapshot). --}}
<section class="steading-turn steading-block" data-season="{{seasons.turnover.next.key}}"
         data-disclosure-row>

	<h3 class="steading-turn-heading">
		{{!-- The season's glyph, tinted to the season it belongs to. Both the image and the tint come
		      from the `data-season` on this section — the stylesheet owns the four paths, because a
		      url() written here would be a document path resolved against the stylesheet, and an
		      install served under a route prefix would 404 on it. --}}
		<button type="button" class="steading-turn-disclosure" data-action="toggleTurn"
		        data-disclosure data-view-state aria-expanded="false"
		        aria-controls="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-turn">
			<i class="fas fa-caret-right stonetop-move-caret" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span class="steading-turn-glyph" aria-hidden="true"></span>
			<span class="steading-turn-title">{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.turnTo"
			      season=(localize seasons.turnover.next.labelKey)}}</span>
		</button>
	</h3>

	<div class="steading-turn-body" id="{{@root.sheetIdPrefix}}-turn" hidden>

		{{!-- The book's harvest plate, floated so the move's own text runs beside it rather than under
		      it. Its silhouette slants up and to the right, so wrapping to its bounding box would
		      leave the wedge on its left blank and break the text against an invisible straight edge;
		      `shape-outside` reads the PNG's own alpha instead and the text follows the art.

		      The path is runtime (the art installer produces it), so it is passed as a custom property
		      here — a url() in the stylesheet cannot take one. Installer-provided and copyrighted, so
		      absent in a world without Book I art: the template asks before it draws. --}}
		{{#if seasons.plate}}
			<img class="steading-seasons-plate" src="{{seasons.plate}}" alt=""
			     style="--plate: url('{{seasons.plate}}')">
		{{/if}}

		{{!-- The move itself, open, above its own steps. The procedure IS this text — "whoever is the
		      most hopeful rolls +Fortunes", "on a 10+, pick 2 seasonal gains" — and it also answers who
		      picks up the dice, which no control on this sheet was saying. The steps below are that
		      text broken into the things the sheet can put a control on. --}}
		{{#if seasons.nextMove}}
			<ul class="steading-turn-move stonetop-unmarked">
				{{> "stonetop.move-row" seasons.nextMove showCheck=false
				    categoryKey=seasons.moves.key allowAdditional=false alwaysShowResource=false
				    disclosure=true startOpen=true}}
			</ul>
		{{else}}
			<p class="stonetop-moves-empty">{{localize "stonetop.steading.seasons.movesEmpty"}}</p>
		{{/if}}

		{{!-- The steps the move carries, in the order it gives them. Read off the move rather than
		      hardcoded: the tab drew Spring's — roll it, pick 1 gain, reset — for all four seasons, so
		      winter's opening 1d4+Population roll had no control and its +Fortunes roll, which is the
		      FOURTH thing winter does, was the one button at the top. --}}
		{{#if seasons.procedure}}
			<ol class="steading-turn-steps">
				{{#each seasons.procedure.steps}}
					{{> "stonetop.steading-turn-step"}}
				{{/each}}
			</ol>
		{{/if}}

	</div>

</section>
